  "body": {
    "id": "thm:simultaneous-graph-confidence-set",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every \\(d\\ge1\\), \\(0<\\alpha\\le1/4\\), and \\(0<\\lambda\\le\\lambda_H\\), put \\(K=\\lceil8\\log(2d/\\alpha)\\rceil\\).  For every \\(n\\ge2K\\), the moment confidence set \\(\\widehat{\\mathcal C}_n^{\\mathrm H}\\) in Definition \\(\\mathrm{def:chart\\text{-}moment\\text{-}rule}\\) is measurable, uses exactly \\(d\\) observable moment queries, has arithmetic cost \\(O(dn)\\), and satisfies\n\\[\n\\inf_{(P,\\theta)\\in\\mathcal M_d^{\\mathrm H}(\\lambda)}\nP^{\\otimes n}\\{\\theta\\in\\widehat{\\mathcal C}_n^{\\mathrm H}\\}\n\\ge1-\\alpha/2.\n\\]\nFor the constant \\(C\\) in Theorem \\(\\mathrm{thm:uniform\\text{-}minimax\\text{-}frontier}\\),\n\\[\nn\\lambda\\ge C\\log\\frac{d+1}{\\alpha}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\inf_{(P,\\theta)\\in\\mathcal M_d^{\\mathrm H}(\\lambda)}\nP^{\\otimes n}\\{\\widehat{\\mathcal C}_n^{\\mathrm H}=\\{\\theta\\}\\}\n\\ge1-\\alpha/2.\n\\]\nConversely, below the constant-factor threshold in Lemma \\(\\mathrm{lem:chart\\text{-}product\\text{-}testing\\text{-}lower}\\), no random set over the same chart class can have both uniform coverage and uniform singleton probability at least \\(1-\\alpha/2\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "d",
      "alpha",
      "lambda",
      "lambdaH",
      "n",
      "P",
      "theta",
      "Mchart",
      "Chat",
