      "thm:uniform-minimax-frontier"
    ],
    "justification": "The confidence set converts the conditional rate theorem into a computable uncertainty object using the same fixed nuisance class and joint regression event, and aligns singleton output with the minimax transition.",
    "gap": "Wang, Kolar, and Drton (2026) give asymptotically valid ordering sets through residual bootstrap, not a finite-sample uniform \\(O(d)\\)-query product set with a matching singleton converse.",
    "consumer": "Applied analysts can report every pair-orientation vector not rejected by the data instead of a single overconfident graph.",
    "proof_tex": "All block boundaries, block averages, lower medians, interval endpoints, Cartesian products, and fallback choices in Definition \\(\\mathrm{def:chart\\text{-}moment\\text{-}rule}\\) are deterministic Borel operations on the sample, so the set is measurable.  One evaluation of \\(\\psi\\) is made for each of the \\(nd\\) observed pairs; block summation and medians add \\(O(dn)\\) arithmetic work and require exactly \\(d\\) coordinatewise moment queries.\n\nThe event \\(\\mathcal E\\) constructed in the proof of Theorem \\(\\mathrm{thm:uniform\\text{-}minimax\\text{-}frontier}\\) has probability at least \\(1-\\alpha/2\\).  On it, the interval centered at \\(\\widehat\\mu_j\\) contains \\(\\mu_j\\).  Lemma \\(\\mathrm{lem:subhalf\\text{-}chart\\text{-}calibration}\\) gives\n\\[\n\\operatorname{sign}(\\mu_j)=\\theta_j,\n\\]\nso the half-line for \\(\\theta_j\\) intersects that interval and \\(\\theta_j\\in B_j\\).  Hence \\(\\theta\\in\\prod_jB_j=\\widehat{\\mathcal C}_n^{\\mathrm H}\\), which proves coverage.  Notice that Lemma \\(\\mathrm{lem:population\\text{-}direction\\text{-}margin}\\) independently gives \\(H_{j,\\theta_j}=0<H_{j,-\\theta_j}\\); thus the moment sign estimates the same causal orientation identified by residual HSIC, rather than defining a new target.\n\nUnder the displayed signal inequality, the radius calculation in the proof of Theorem \\(\\mathrm{thm:uniform\\text{-}minimax\\text{-}frontier}\\) gives \\(2\\rho<|\\mu_j|\\) for every \\(j\\).  On \\(\\mathcal E\\) the whole interval then has sign \\(\\theta_j\\), so \\(B_j=\\{\\theta_j\\}\\) for all \\(j\\).  This proves the singleton guarantee.  The final assertion is exactly the random-set part of Lemma \\(\\mathrm{lem:chart\\text{-}product\\text{-}testing\\text{-}lower}\\), on the identical chart class and with the identical confidence level.",
